# Figma personal access token — SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Generate at:
# https://www.figma.com/developers/api#access-tokens
#
# The web app's /api/import route (and asset export via the Images API) uses
# this key on the server; it is never sent to the browser or logged. The
# hosted deployment uses the deployer's key — visitors cannot supply their
# own token. To import your own Figma files, run the app locally with this
# set in apps/web/.env.local, or use the CLI (`forgeui generate`) with
# FIGMA_API_KEY in your shell environment.
FIGMA_API_KEY=your_figma_personal_access_token_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live-import authorization (see apps/web/lib/import-guard.ts)
#
# /api/import fetches a Figma file with the key above. To stop anonymous
# visitors from using your key to read arbitrary files or burn your quota,
# live import is DISABLED BY DEFAULT. The sample workspace still works without
# any of this (it loads a committed fixture client-side). Choose ONE:
#
#   1. Allowlist (recommended for public demos): only these file keys import.
#      FIGMA_ALLOWED_FILE_KEYS=key1,key2
#
#   2. Open (trusted/private deployments only): allow any file key the token
#      can reach. Still rate limited.
#      FIGMA_IMPORT_PUBLIC=true
#
# Leave both unset to keep live import disabled (the secure default).
# FIGMA_ALLOWED_FILE_KEYS=
# FIGMA_IMPORT_PUBLIC=false
